---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"The One-Page Loan Summary for a Problem Hotel Loan"} description={"How a community bank presents a problem hotel loan: thirteen headings in the words credit officers already use, and what each one tells a buyer."}>
  <Hero eyebrow="For community banks" title={"How a community bank presents a problem loan."} lead={"Put the loan on one page, under these headings, in your own words, and we can respond."} />
  <SectionNav section="communityBanks" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">The one-page summary</p><h2>Thirteen headings, in the order a bank usually writes them.</h2>
        <p>This is the page the conversation starts from. A full file is not needed yet. Send it under a confidentiality agreement: we sign yours or provide ours.</p></div>
      <div class="table-scroll"><table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Heading</th><th scope="col">What goes under it</th><th scope="col">Why we ask</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody><tr><th scope="row">Borrower and guarantor(s)</th><td>The legal name of the borrower, and each guarantor with the type of guaranty: full, limited, or carve-out.</td><td>Who is obligated, and what a guaranty adds to the recovery.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Property</th><td>Hotel name, flag, city and state, number of rooms (keys), year built, and service level: limited-service, select-service, extended-stay, or full-service.</td><td>The collateral, and the comp set it competes in.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Loan</th><td>Original amount and origination date, principal balance, accrued interest, interest rate (and the default rate, if charged), maturity date, and loan type, including SBA or USDA if guaranteed.</td><td>The numbers any price starts from.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Status</th><td>Current or past due since a date, days past due, non-accrual date, whether the loan has matured, and the date of the last payment.</td><td>How far along the default is.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Risk rating</th><td>The current risk rating (special mention, substandard, doubtful) and the date it changed.</td><td>How the bank classifies the loan today.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Collateral and lien position</th><td>First mortgage or first deed of trust, assignment of rents, security interest in furniture, fixtures, and equipment and in accounts, and any junior lien or ground lease.</td><td>What the bank actually holds.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Valuation</th><td>The most recent appraisal: as-is value, date, and appraiser. Or an evaluation, or a broker opinion of value.</td><td>Where the bank's own view of value comes from.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Reserve and charge-offs</th><td>The specific reserve and any charge-offs to date, and the carrying value. Optional at this stage: share it if the bank is comfortable doing so.</td><td>So a price can be discussed against the right number.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Flag and operations</th><td>Flag in good standing, or a notice received. Improvement plan outstanding or not, with the cost and deadline. Owner-operated or managed. T-12 revenue and NOI, and RevPAR against the comp set, if available.</td><td>The hotel as a business.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Participations and guarantees</th><td>Participations sold or held, as lead or participant, and the consents a sale needs. A government guarantee, with the agency and the percentage.</td><td>Who has to agree to a loan sale.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Legal status</th><td>Foreclosure filed or not, receiver appointed or not, borrower bankruptcy, and any litigation or claims by the borrower.</td><td>Where the case stands.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Workout history</th><td>Modifications, extensions, and forbearance agreements, with what was promised and what was kept.</td><td>How the borrower has performed, and where past efforts stopped.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">What the bank wants</th><td>Timing, whether the bank is open to a discounted payoff or a deed in lieu with the borrower, and any party already interested.</td><td>What a good outcome looks like for the bank.</td></tr></tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">In your words</p><h2>Write it the way the bank already does.</h2>
        <p>We read whatever the bank writes. This is how we write it back to you, so that the terms stay the same from the first page to the loan sale agreement.</p></div>
      <div class="table-scroll" data-terms="variants"><table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">We write</th><th scope="col">You may write</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody><tr><th scope="row">loan sale</th><td>note sale, loan disposition</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">principal balance</th><td>outstanding balance, outstanding principal, UPB</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">past due</th><td>delinquent, DPD</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">non-accrual</th><td>nonaccrual, NA status</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">risk rating</th><td>grade, risk grade, classification</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">problem loan</th><td>troubled loan, distressed loan</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">special assets</th><td>workout group, special credits, problem asset management</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">reserve</th><td>allowance, ACL allocation, ALLL</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">charge-off</th><td>write-down</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">OREO</th><td>ORE, other real estate owned, REO</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">flag</th><td>brand, franchise, affiliation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">comp set</th><td>competitive set</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">T-12</th><td>trailing twelve months</td></tr></tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="wrap intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">What can wait</p><h2>The first page does not need to carry everything.</h2></div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div><dt>The borrower's personal information</dt><dd>Personal financial statements, tax returns, and similar customer information can wait for diligence, and for the consent the bank needs to share it. A loan sale involves information the bank is obliged to protect.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>The full credit file</dt><dd>The note, mortgage, assignments, and guaranties come at diligence. The <a class="more arrow" href="/banks/information-to-send/">full list is here</a>.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Anything you do not know yet</dt><dd>Say what is missing. A gap that is named is easier to price than one that is not mentioned.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/banks/information-to-send/">What to send, and when <span>Banks</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#risk-rating">Risk rating <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#past-due">Past due <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#upb">Unpaid principal balance (UPB) <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#oreo">OREO (other real estate owned) <span>Glossary</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Discuss a hotel loan in confidence."} text={"A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell."} label={"Start a conversation"} />
</Base>
